The issue asks to move `reqwest/rustls` from `reqwest` to `reqwest_rustls`. This hunk rewrites identity test provisioning instead:
- it gates on a new Bicep output;
- it adds readiness polling and endpoint auth checks that fail the whole provisioning step;
- it uses temporary kubeconfig files;
- it deletes the pod on every run;
- it changes parameter mandatoriness.

It ships alongside removing the `CI_HAS_DEPLOYED_RESOURCES` skip from the ACI/AKS live tests. So in a live CI run with `deployResources=false`, this script now returns early. `IDENTITY_ACI_IP_USER_ASSIGNED`/`IDENTITY_AKS_IP` are never published, and those live tests panic instead of skipping.

Split this infrastructure change into its own PR, or keep the test skip guard.
